    thinking: "**Verifying Key Components**\n\nI\'m now deep in the process of thoroughly verifying the crucial components: `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `/src/engine/CameraController.ts`, `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`, `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, and `/src/App.tsx`. I\'m meticulously checking every detail to ensure everything aligns perfectly.\n\n\n**Analyzing Joystick State**\n\nI\'ve been examining the virtual joystick state within `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` in great detail. I\'ve focused on how `joystickX` and `joystickY` are handled, particularly concerning scaling during viewport resizing. Specifically, I am ensuring that the normalized radial position of the joystick remains consistent across any resolution change, while `aimCursorX` and `aimCursorY` always remain within their correct boundaries.\n\n\n**Refining Boundary Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the boundary handling for the virtual joystick within `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`. Specifically, I\'ve implemented a robust clamping mechanism, ensuring that `candX` and `candY` are immediately constrained within `this.aimBoundary` using `clampToRoundedRect`. This approach guarantees that the joystick remains pinned to the perimeter, enabling smooth sliding along edges and corners without any lag, even when the mouse goes past the boundary. Finally, the clamped values are stored in `this.joystickX` and `this.joystickY`. I\'m now testing the radial response to make sure it functions as planned.\n\n\n**Calculating Angular Rates**\n\nI\'m now calculating angular rates. I am leveraging `joystickEval` to derive `steerX`, `steerY`, and other control variables. Then, I\'m integrating independent yaw and pitch target rates, applying sensitivity settings and keyboard input. I am ensuring that the ship\'s yaw and pitch are safely handled, by clamping these values. Finally, I\'m modeling angular acceleration and damping, using a ship agility factor derived from its profile, to determine how fast the ship can maneuver safely.\n\n\n"
