  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Test Results**\n\nI\'m stunned! My real browser test just uncovered a sneaky bug within `test6_smoothReturn` that appeared under low FPS conditions (SwiftShader at 3 FPS). This also exposed something else entirely.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Accumulation**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core of the problem in `test6_smoothReturn`. The critical issue is how `InputManager` accumulates mouse deltas and the effect of low frame rates. It\'s clear that queued mouse deltas from the loop aren\'t fully consumed before subsequent `sendMouseDelta` calls, leading to a lingering delta within the frame buffer that causes incorrect clamping of the final `candidateX` value. I am considering potential fixes.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Jy__armJJdeR_uMPkvXpwQY"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11412862723790625097"
