  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Chromium\'s Data**\n\nWow! These Chromium execution numbers are incredible. The deadzone data, perfectly aligns with our expectations. It\'s textbook! Seeing how the steering values and yaw velocity are handled in that zone is validating our understanding. It\'s a goldmine of information.\n\n\n**Confirming Zero Drift**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the expected zero-drift behavior, observing that `pitchVelocity`, `headingDeg`, and `pitchDeg` all remain at zero. This observation is extremely encouraging and aligns precisely with the design specifications. The system is starting from a perfect state!\n\n\n**Observing Joystick Return**\n\nI\'m seeing incredible responsiveness! The inward joystick movement, after a large outward push, registers a value drop and yaw change in a single frame. The values converge almost perfectly to the expected rate with no significant delay. Returning the joystick to zero dampens yaw, and settles virtually at zero heading with no overshoot. I\'m noting the immediate adjustment confirms the fast response time.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "tS__auaZKfnx-8YP7N7CmAM"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4956526392731300258"
      name: "view_file"
