  planner_response {
    response: "STARFALL\'s mouse flight control has been redesigned around a **Virtual Joystick** input architecture while preserving the existing Pointer Lock implementation (`InputManager` unchanged).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Previous Input Architecture & Its Problems\n- **Unbounded excess accumulation with hidden state**: Relative mouse movement accumulated into an unbounded virtual aim coordinate past the aiming boundary (using soft outward compression and an asymmetric `inwardExcessReturnFactor` unwind hack). Even while the visual reticle was pinned to the boundary edge, invisible outward excess kept changing the turn rate and caused asymmetric inward vs. outward feel.\n- **Non-monotonic three-zone sensitivity jump**: Inside the `40% \303\227 45%` boundary, sensitivity was `0.50x`, then dropped sharply to `0.30x` (`boundarySensitivity`) upon crossing the edge before surging nonlinearly via `f(e) = e\302\262 / (1 + e\302\262)` up to `1.80x` (`maxSensitivity`). Moving farther outward briefly *slowed* turning before spiking, and holding outward continued ramping sensitivity beyond the boundary instead of capping predictably.\n- **Oversized boundary & square/axis-separated deadzone**: The `40% \303\227 45%` boundary required wide mouse sweeps, and independent per-axis deadzones caused sticky axis snapping rather than smooth radial steering.\n- **Coupled yaw/pitch & single-pole smoothing**: Yaw and pitch shared sensitivity multipliers, and angular velocity used a single exponential lerp without separate angular acceleration and stopping-damping control.\n\n---\n\n### 2. New Virtual Joystick Architecture\n- **Preserved Pointer Lock**: `InputManager` continues using the Pointer Lock API with pure relative `movementX` / `movementY`, single-event accumulation per frame, zero cursor recentering, and no reliance on absolute cursor coordinates.\n- **Bounded Logical Displacement**: Relative mouse deltas scale by `mouseSensitivity` and a viewport-height normalization factor (`clamp(vh / 720, 0.5, 2.5)`) so physical desk travel remains consistent across resolutions. Each frame, the logical joystick vector `(joystickX, joystickY)` is immediately projected onto the centered rounded-rectangle boundary via C1-continuous closest-point clamping (`clampToRoundedRect`).\n  - Pushing past the boundary keeps logical displacement cleanly on the perimeter (sliding smoothly along edges and rounded corners) without runaway sensitivity or hidden excess.\n  - Pulling inward immediately moves the joystick inward on the very first frame with zero unwind lag.\n- **Exact Ray-to-Perimeter Radial Normalization**: `computeRoundedRectRayRadius` computes the exact distance `R(\316\270)` from center to the rounded-rectangle perimeter along the current joystick ray so every point on both straight edges and rounded corners normalizes smoothly to `r = 1.0`.\n- **Decoupled Camera Follow**: `CameraController` remains strictly decoupled from mouse sensitivity and ship rotation ownership; chase tracking rates were tightened slightly (`posLambda: 12.5`, `rotLambda: 15.5`, `upAlpha: 10.5`) and lateral turn offset was decoupled from `cameraSensitivity` so higher camera follow produces tighter tracking rather than extra lag.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Boundary Dimensions\n- **Base Width**: `30%` of viewport width (`aimBoundaryWidth: 0.30`)\n- **Base Height**: `35%` of viewport height (`aimBoundaryHeight: 0.35`)\n- **Shape & Alignment**: Centered rounded rectangle with corner radius `30%` of `min(halfW, halfH)` (`aimBoundaryCornerRadius: 0.30`)\n- **Configurable Scaling**: Scaled uniformly via **Joystick Radius** (`joystickRadius`, default `1.00`, range `0.65`\342\200\223`1.50`), with automatic viewport resize recalculation and proportional joystick-position preservation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Deadzone & Response Curve\n- **Center Radial Deadzone**: `deadzone: 0.06` (`6%` of joystick radius, configurable `0%`\342\200\223`20%`). Outputs exact `0` for `r \342\211\244 deadzone`, rendered with a subtle centered deadzone indicator on the HUD.\n- **Smooth Conservative Radial Curve**: For `r > deadzone`, `u = (r - deadzone) / (1 - deadzone)` maps through:\n  `output(r) = clamp(u^p * (k + (1 - k) * u\302\262 * (3 - 2u)), 0, 1) * maxSteeringInput`\n  - `responseCurve` (`p`): default **`1.35`** (configurable `1.00`\342\200\223`2.40`)\n  - `precisionSensitivity` (`k`): **`0.85`** (separated in config; gently calms center micro-aiming while blending smoothly to `1.0` at the perimeter)\n  - `maxSteeringInput`: **`1.0`** (strictly capped at/beyond `r = 1.0`; provably monotonic across the full range with zero discontinuities at deadzone or boundary).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final Yaw & Pitch Settings\nSeparated and independently adjustable in Settings (with `Restore Defaults` and `starfall.settings.v6` migration):\n- **Mouse Sensitivity**: `1.00x` (`0.30x`\342\200\223`2.50x`)\n- **Joystick Radius**: `100%` / `30% \303\227 35%` (`65%`\342\200\223`150%`)\n- **Deadzone**: `6%` (`0%`\342\200\223`20%`)\n- **Yaw Sensitivity (`yawRate`)**: **`1.00x`** (`0.40x`\342\200\223`1.80x`) \342\206\222 `2.10 rad/s` (`~120.3\302\260/s`) max yaw on Interceptor\n- **Pitch Sensitivity (`pitchRate`)**: **`0.90x`** (`0.40x`\342\200\223`1.80x`) \342\206\222 `1.755 rad/s` (`~100.6\302\260/s`) max pitch on Interceptor (balanced for widescreen vertical travel)\n- **Response Curve**: **`1.35`** (`1.00`\342\200\223`2.40`)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Changes to Angular Acceleration & Damping\nReplaced the previous single-pole `angularSmoothing` + `recoverySmoothing` pipeline with a dedicated delta-time `stepAngularVelocity` model scaled by hull maneuverability (`profile.angularDamping / 7.5`):\n- **Angular Acceleration (`angularAcceleration`)**: **`18.0 rad/s\302\262`** \342\200\224 smooths abrupt full-deflection slams without clipping micro-corrections.\n- **Angular Damping (`angularDamping`)**: **`14.0 s\342\201\273\302\271`** (~`71 ms` tracking time constant) for responsive turn engagement with minimal latency.\n- **Stopping Damping Boost (`stoppingDampingBoost`)**: **`1.25\303\227`** (`17.5 s\342\201\273\302\271` when decelerating toward center or reversing direction) so returning the mouse to center halts turning cleanly without drift or overshoot.\n- Roll (`A`/`D`), boost, thrust, passive drag, lateral grip, and visual banking retain Phase 1 flight feel.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Actual Browser Testing Results\nVerified live in headless Chromium (CDP against `http://localhost:3000` with WebGL active) alongside `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build`:\n- **Settings UI & Restore Defaults**: All 6 Virtual Joystick sliders and the updated live response curve graph rendered cleanly (`Mouse Sensitivity`, `Joystick Radius`, `Deadzone`, `Response Curve`, `Yaw Sensitivity`, `Pitch Sensitivity`). Changing `Mouse Sensitivity` to `1.85x` and clicking `Restore Defaults` restored all defaults cleanly.\n- **Center Deadzone**: Micro-movement `(+6px, -3px)` (`r = 0.0314 < 0.06`) remained in `\'deadzone\'` with `steerX = 0`, `steerY = 0`, `yawVelocity = 0`, `pitchVelocity = 0`, and `0.00\302\260` heading drift.\n- **Small Precise Steering**: `+32px` movement (`r = 0.1667`) entered `\'active\'` with gentle `steerX = 0.0453` and smooth low-rate yaw.\n- **Progressive Curve Sweep (1280\303\227720, `halfW = 192px`)**:\n  - `25%` (`48px`): `steerX = 0.1000`, settled `yawVelocity = -0.2093 rad/s`\n  - `50%` (`96px`): `steerX = 0.3294`, settled `yawVelocity = -0.6891 rad/s`\n  - `75%` (`144px`): `steerX = 0.6415`, settled `yawVelocity = -1.3422 rad/s`\n  - `100%` (`192px`): `steerX = 1.0000`, settled `yawVelocity = -2.0911 rad/s` (`zone = \'max\'`)\n- **Boundary Clamp, Continuous Turning & Display-Edge Persistence**: Pushing `+1440px` further outward (exceeding the `1280px` viewport width) kept `joystickX` strictly bounded at `192.00px`, `steerX = 1.0`, and constant max turn rate `-2.1000 rad/s` while continuously advancing ship heading by `+72.2\302\260`.\n- **Immediate Smooth Return Inward**: Immediately sending `-60px` after `+1440px` outward dropped `joystickX` from `192px` to `132px` in a single frame (`r = 0.6875`, `steerX = 0.5571`, `yawVelocity` smoothly stepping `-2.10 \342\206\222 -1.56 \342\206\222 -1.17 rad/s`). Returning to center damped `yawVelocity` cleanly to `-0.0004 rad/s`.\n- **Independent Pitch & Rounded Corner Arc**: Full vertical `-160px` clamped to `-126px` (`pitchVelocity = 1.7534 rad/s`, `pitchDeg = +45.32\302\260`); diagonal `(+240px, +180px)` projected onto the exact circular corner arc `(180.01, 115.82)` at `r = 1.0`, `|steer| = 1.0`.\n- **Pointer Lock & Viewport Resizing**: Verified synchronous `canvas.requestPointerLock()` invocation on click; tested `1280\303\227720` (`384\303\227252`), `1920\303\2271080` (`576\303\227378`), `1024\303\227768` (`307.2\303\227268.8`), and `800\303\227600` (`240\303\227210`) \342\200\224 both engine geometry and live HUD SVG matched exact `30% \303\227 35%` rounded-rectangle dimensions at every size.\n- **Visual & Runtime Stability**: Inspected rendered Settings and live flight HUD screenshots (active steering and max-boundary turning); `0` console or runtime errors.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Remaining Issues / Notes\n- Headless Chromium runs on SwiftShader software WebGL (~2\342\200\2233 FPS in headless CI) and does not grant an OS-level hardware pointer lock without a physical cursor; real-hardware 60 FPS subjective feel (fine mouse DPI calibration across different physical mice and high-refresh monitors) should be spot-checked interactively during live desktop playtesting.\n- Future tunable option if desired: exposing an optional toggle for gentle auto-recenter assist when the mouse is idle (currently omitted intentionally so holding the joystick outward maintains continuous turning cleanly)."
    message_id: "3S__aojDM93K_PUPk6XIgQI"
    modified_response: "STARFALL\'s mouse flight control has been redesigned around a **Virtual Joystick** input architecture while preserving the existing Pointer Lock implementation (`InputManager` unchanged).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Previous Input Architecture & Its Problems\n- **Unbounded excess accumulation with hidden state**: Relative mouse movement accumulated into an unbounded virtual aim coordinate past the aiming boundary (using soft outward compression and an asymmetric `inwardExcessReturnFactor` unwind hack). Even while the visual reticle was pinned to the boundary edge, invisible outward excess kept changing the turn rate and caused asymmetric inward vs. outward feel.\n- **Non-monotonic three-zone sensitivity jump**: Inside the `40% \303\227 45%` boundary, sensitivity was `0.50x`, then dropped sharply to `0.30x` (`boundarySensitivity`) upon crossing the edge before surging nonlinearly via `f(e) = e\302\262 / (1 + e\302\262)` up to `1.80x` (`maxSensitivity`). Moving farther outward briefly *slowed* turning before spiking, and holding outward continued ramping sensitivity beyond the boundary instead of capping predictably.\n- **Oversized boundary & square/axis-separated deadzone**: The `40% \303\227 45%` boundary required wide mouse sweeps, and independent per-axis deadzones caused sticky axis snapping rather than smooth radial steering.\n- **Coupled yaw/pitch & single-pole smoothing**: Yaw and pitch shared sensitivity multipliers, and angular velocity used a single exponential lerp without separate angular acceleration and stopping-damping control.\n\n---\n\n### 2. New Virtual Joystick Architecture\n- **Preserved Pointer Lock**: `InputManager` continues using the Pointer Lock API with pure relative `movementX` / `movementY`, single-event accumulation per frame, zero cursor recentering, and no reliance on absolute cursor coordinates.\n- **Bounded Logical Displacement**: Relative mouse deltas scale by `mouseSensitivity` and a viewport-height normalization factor (`clamp(vh / 720, 0.5, 2.5)`) so physical desk travel remains consistent across resolutions. Each frame, the logical joystick vector `(joystickX, joystickY)` is immediately projected onto the centered rounded-rectangle boundary via C1-continuous closest-point clamping (`clampToRoundedRect`).\n  - Pushing past the boundary keeps logical displacement cleanly on the perimeter (sliding smoothly along edges and rounded corners) without runaway sensitivity or hidden excess.\n  - Pulling inward immediately moves the joystick inward on the very first frame with zero unwind lag.\n- **Exact Ray-to-Perimeter Radial Normalization**: `computeRoundedRectRayRadius` computes the exact distance `R(\316\270)` from center to the rounded-rectangle perimeter along the current joystick ray so every point on both straight edges and rounded corners normalizes smoothly to `r = 1.0`.\n- **Decoupled Camera Follow**: `CameraController` remains strictly decoupled from mouse sensitivity and ship rotation ownership; chase tracking rates were tightened slightly (`posLambda: 12.5`, `rotLambda: 15.5`, `upAlpha: 10.5`) and lateral turn offset was decoupled from `cameraSensitivity` so higher camera follow produces tighter tracking rather than extra lag.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Boundary Dimensions\n- **Base Width**: `30%` of viewport width (`aimBoundaryWidth: 0.30`)\n- **Base Height**: `35%` of viewport height (`aimBoundaryHeight: 0.35`)\n- **Shape & Alignment**: Centered rounded rectangle with corner radius `30%` of `min(halfW, halfH)` (`aimBoundaryCornerRadius: 0.30`)\n- **Configurable Scaling**: Scaled uniformly via **Joystick Radius** (`joystickRadius`, default `1.00`, range `0.65`\342\200\223`1.50`), with automatic viewport resize recalculation and proportional joystick-position preservation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Deadzone & Response Curve\n- **Center Radial Deadzone**: `deadzone: 0.06` (`6%` of joystick radius, configurable `0%`\342\200\223`20%`). Outputs exact `0` for `r \342\211\244 deadzone`, rendered with a subtle centered deadzone indicator on the HUD.\n- **Smooth Conservative Radial Curve**: For `r > deadzone`, `u = (r - deadzone) / (1 - deadzone)` maps through:\n  `output(r) = clamp(u^p * (k + (1 - k) * u\302\262 * (3 - 2u)), 0, 1) * maxSteeringInput`\n  - `responseCurve` (`p`): default **`1.35`** (configurable `1.00`\342\200\223`2.40`)\n  - `precisionSensitivity` (`k`): **`0.85`** (separated in config; gently calms center micro-aiming while blending smoothly to `1.0` at the perimeter)\n  - `maxSteeringInput`: **`1.0`** (strictly capped at/beyond `r = 1.0`; provably monotonic across the full range with zero discontinuities at deadzone or boundary).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Final Yaw & Pitch Settings\nSeparated and independently adjustable in Settings (with `Restore Defaults` and `starfall.settings.v6` migration):\n- **Mouse Sensitivity**: `1.00x` (`0.30x`\342\200\223`2.50x`)\n- **Joystick Radius**: `100%` / `30% \303\227 35%` (`65%`\342\200\223`150%`)\n- **Deadzone**: `6%` (`0%`\342\200\223`20%`)\n- **Yaw Sensitivity (`yawRate`)**: **`1.00x`** (`0.40x`\342\200\223`1.80x`) \342\206\222 `2.10 rad/s` (`~120.3\302\260/s`) max yaw on Interceptor\n- **Pitch Sensitivity (`pitchRate`)**: **`0.90x`** (`0.40x`\342\200\223`1.80x`) \342\206\222 `1.755 rad/s` (`~100.6\302\260/s`) max pitch on Interceptor (balanced for widescreen vertical travel)\n- **Response Curve**: **`1.35`** (`1.00`\342\200\223`2.40`)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Changes to Angular Acceleration & Damping\nReplaced the previous single-pole `angularSmoothing` + `recoverySmoothing` pipeline with a dedicated delta-time `stepAngularVelocity` model scaled by hull maneuverability (`profile.angularDamping / 7.5`):\n- **Angular Acceleration (`angularAcceleration`)**: **`18.0 rad/s\302\262`** \342\200\224 smooths abrupt full-deflection slams without clipping micro-corrections.\n- **Angular Damping (`angularDamping`)**: **`14.0 s\342\201\273\302\271`** (~`71 ms` tracking time constant) for responsive turn engagement with minimal latency.\n- **Stopping Damping Boost (`stoppingDampingBoost`)**: **`1.25\303\227`** (`17.5 s\342\201\273\302\271` when decelerating toward center or reversing direction) so returning the mouse to center halts turning cleanly without drift or overshoot.\n- Roll (`A`/`D`), boost, thrust, passive drag, lateral grip, and visual banking retain Phase 1 flight feel.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Actual Browser Testing Results\nVerified live in headless Chromium (CDP against `http://localhost:3000` with WebGL active) alongside `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build`:\n- **Settings UI & Restore Defaults**: All 6 Virtual Joystick sliders and the updated live response curve graph rendered cleanly (`Mouse Sensitivity`, `Joystick Radius`, `Deadzone`, `Response Curve`, `Yaw Sensitivity`, `Pitch Sensitivity`). Changing `Mouse Sensitivity` to `1.85x` and clicking `Restore Defaults` restored all defaults cleanly.\n- **Center Deadzone**: Micro-movement `(+6px, -3px)` (`r = 0.0314 < 0.06`) remained in `\'deadzone\'` with `steerX = 0`, `steerY = 0`, `yawVelocity = 0`, `pitchVelocity = 0`, and `0.00\302\260` heading drift.\n- **Small Precise Steering**: `+32px` movement (`r = 0.1667`) entered `\'active\'` with gentle `steerX = 0.0453` and smooth low-rate yaw.\n- **Progressive Curve Sweep (1280\303\227720, `halfW = 192px`)**:\n  - `25%` (`48px`): `steerX = 0.1000`, settled `yawVelocity = -0.2093 rad/s`\n  - `50%` (`96px`): `steerX = 0.3294`, settled `yawVelocity = -0.6891 rad/s`\n  - `75%` (`144px`): `steerX = 0.6415`, settled `yawVelocity = -1.3422 rad/s`\n  - `100%` (`192px`): `steerX = 1.0000`, settled `yawVelocity = -2.0911 rad/s` (`zone = \'max\'`)\n- **Boundary Clamp, Continuous Turning & Display-Edge Persistence**: Pushing `+1440px` further outward (exceeding the `1280px` viewport width) kept `joystickX` strictly bounded at `192.00px`, `steerX = 1.0`, and constant max turn rate `-2.1000 rad/s` while continuously advancing ship heading by `+72.2\302\260`.\n- **Immediate Smooth Return Inward**: Immediately sending `-60px` after `+1440px` outward dropped `joystickX` from `192px` to `132px` in a single frame (`r = 0.6875`, `steerX = 0.5571`, `yawVelocity` smoothly stepping `-2.10 \342\206\222 -1.56 \342\206\222 -1.17 rad/s`). Returning to center damped `yawVelocity` cleanly to `-0.0004 rad/s`.\n- **Independent Pitch & Rounded Corner Arc**: Full vertical `-160px` clamped to `-126px` (`pitchVelocity = 1.7534 rad/s`, `pitchDeg = +45.32\302\260`); diagonal `(+240px, +180px)` projected onto the exact circular corner arc `(180.01, 115.82)` at `r = 1.0`, `|steer| = 1.0`.\n- **Pointer Lock & Viewport Resizing**: Verified synchronous `canvas.requestPointerLock()` invocation on click; tested `1280\303\227720` (`384\303\227252`), `1920\303\2271080` (`576\303\227378`), `1024\303\227768` (`307.2\303\227268.8`), and `800\303\227600` (`240\303\227210`) \342\200\224 both engine geometry and live HUD SVG matched exact `30% \303\227 35%` rounded-rectangle dimensions at every size.\n- **Visual & Runtime Stability**: Inspected rendered Settings and live flight HUD screenshots (active steering and max-boundary turning); `0` console or runtime errors.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Remaining Issues / Notes\n- Headless Chromium runs on SwiftShader software WebGL (~2\342\200\2233 FPS in headless CI) and does not grant an OS-level hardware pointer lock without a physical cursor; real-hardware 60 FPS subjective feel (fine mouse DPI calibration across different physical mice and high-refresh monitors) should be spot-checked interactively during live desktop playtesting.\n- Future tunable option if desired: exposing an optional toggle for gentle auto-recenter assist when the mouse is idle (currently omitted intentionally so holding the joystick outward maintains continuous turning cleanly)."
