  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Deprecation Warnings**\n\nI\'m currently focused on eliminating the `THREE.Clock` deprecation warning in `@react-three/fiber@9.8.2`. I\'m comparing the two potential solutions by examining `node_modules/@react-three/fiber/dist/events-.*.js` to get a surgical fix.\n\n\n**Exploring Compatibility Module**\n\nI\'m now investigating a clean solution to address the deprecation. I\'m considering creating a compatibility module using `THREE.Timer` as a `THREE.Clock` adapter. This approach promises a genuine engineering solution without resorting to hacks or direct modifications of `node_modules`. I aim for a minimal, clearly defined module that preserves the `Clock` interface. This should give us a super clean solution!\n\n\n**Defining Timer Clock Interface**\n\nI\'m now deep diving into the `TimerClock`\'s methods: `elapsedTime`, `oldTime`, `running`, `autoStart`, `start()`, `stop()`, `getDelta()`, and `getElapsedTime()`. I\'m focusing on how this can seamlessly replace the deprecated `THREE.Clock` functionality, and how to replicate the timer functionality.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "OjD_aoiqCcb3jrEP0eHxyAM"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1246381816749697039"
