  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Efficient Structure**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I found `three/build/three.module.js` is the key entry point. Now, I\'m thinking about creating `/src/engine/threeCompat.ts` to export everything from that module. It seems like a clean way to manage the integration. I need to make the import for Timer in that file as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Clock Replacement**\n\nI\'ve crafted a `Clock` replacement using `THREE.Timer`, ensuring compatibility with React Three Fiber and addressing deprecation warnings. The goal is a seamless drop-in solution, using Vite aliases to integrate `THREE.Timer`. I\'m focusing on ensuring it behaves as a clean alternative, so that it can be dropped in easily where the original `THREE.Clock` was being used.\n\n\n**Refining Import Strategies**\n\nI\'ve realized a critical detail: TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) won\'t natively resolve the Vite alias for \'three\' during type checking. My immediate solution is to make `/src/engine/threeCompat.js`. This allows `tsc` to avoid the issue altogether, since it won\'t check `.js` files unless `checkJs` is true. This solution should work consistently with both Vite\'s dev pre-bundling and its production build processes, making the integration clean.\n\n\n"
