  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Timer Methods**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the `Timer` class, specifically the interaction between `reset()` and `update()`. It seems `reset()` establishes a baseline by setting `_currentTime`. Then, `update()` calculates a delta using `_currentTime`, and previous values, to track elapsed time. I\'m aiming to understand the time-keeping mechanism and how it impacts overall performance.\n\n\n**Refining Timer Implementation**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the delta calculation within the timer. It seems `timer.getDelta()` precisely delivers the time difference in seconds. I discovered the Page Visibility API delta-spike protection, if `timer.connect(document)` is invoked in `start()`. I\'m now verifying that `graphics.shadows` is a boolean in `src/config/graphics.ts`, ensuring direct R3F configuration of `THREE.PCFShadowMap`. I\'m preparing to apply some clean edits based on these findings.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "WTD_aoKfLITVjMcPrtTtoAY"
