  planner_response {
    response: "Both Three.js r187 warnings have been fixed and verified with zero console warnings or errors in Chromium:\n\n- **`PCFSoftShadowMap` warning**: Updated the R3F `<Canvas>` `shadows` prop from boolean (`shadows={graphics.shadows}`, which causes React Three Fiber to assign the removed `THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap`) to `shadows={graphics.shadows ? \'percentage\' : false}`, which configures `THREE.PCFShadowMap` directly.\n- **`THREE.Clock` deprecation warning**: Added a `THREE.Timer`-backed `Clock` compatibility module (`src/engine/threeCompat.js`) wired via Vite\'s `resolve.alias`, so `@react-three/fiber`\'s internal store initialization runs on `THREE.Timer` instead of instantiating the deprecated `THREE.Clock`.\n\n**Verification**:\n- `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both succeeded cleanly.\n- Headless Chromium verification from startup through launching Mission 01 into active 3D flight reported `0` warnings and `0` errors."
